{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>I said I would scatter them.</b> 'אפאיהם' — I would scatter them to every corner. And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote: 'I said' — the will was, before they would be thus forever scattered to every corner, that their memory would be forgotten from mankind, were it not for the wrath of the enemy. And this alludes to the exile of the ten tribes who were exiled to the river Gozan, which the sages call the river Sambatyon. And it is called Gozan from the root of (Numbers 11:31) ״ויגז שלוים״, (Psalms 71:6) ״אתה גוזי״, for those who stand behind it are cut off from the children of men, and they call it Sambatyon because of its resting on the Sabbath, for the day of Sabbath in that language is 'sabat,' also in Arabic, and it is customary in their language to add 'yon' to epithets, like 'ezovyon,' 'moliyon,' 'huriyon,' and so many others — up to here are the words of the Rav, of blessed memory. <b>And even though</b> the Torah spoke of this only in allusion and in brief, we have an explanation from the words of our sages, of blessed memory, in scattered places. That is, it says in Bereshit Rabbah, parashat Vayetze Ya'akov: Rabbi Yehudah son of R. Shimon said, 'Not to the place where the ten tribes were exiled were Judah and Benjamin exiled; for the ten tribes were exiled beyond the river Sambatyon, while Judah and Benjamin are scattered in all the lands.' <b>And in the Midrash on</b> Song of Songs (Song of Songs 1:16), ״אף ערשנו רעננה״ — these are the ten tribes who were exiled beyond the river Sambatyon. <b>And in the Yerushalmi</b> of Sanhedrin, chapter Chelek: 'Three exiles did Israel go into — one beyond the river Sambatyon, one to the Daphne of Antioch, and one where a cloud descended and covered them. And just as they went into three exiles, so did the tribes of Reuben, Gad, and the half-tribe of Manasseh go into three exiles; what is the reason? (Ezekiel 23:31) ״בדרך אחותך הלכה ונתת כוסה בידך״. And when they return, they return from the three exiles, as it is said (Isaiah 49:9) ״לאמר לאסורים צאו״ — these are those exiled beyond the river Sambatyon; ״לאשר בחשך הגלו״ — these are those upon whom the cloud descended and covered them; ״על דרכים ירעו״ — these are those exiled to the Daphne of Antioch.' <b>And in the Tosefta</b> of Sanhedrin: 'Rabbi says: the ten tribes have a share in the world to come, as it is said (ibid. v. 27) ״והיה ביום ההוא יתקע וגו׳ והנדחים בארץ מצרים״ — these are the ten tribes.' And in Torat Kohanim it says: (Leviticus 26:38) ״ואבדתם בגוים״ — Rabbi Akiva says: these are the ten tribes who were exiled to Media.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:28.908575441Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}